AB  - Prototype-based classifiers represent each class with a high-dimensional prototype vector. However, existing methods generate prototypes in a manner that is inconsistent with how real samples are embedded, leading to mismatched feature distributions and unreliable confidence estimates. To address this issue, we propose Template Representation Learning (TRL), which uses representative template images and embeds both templates and samples through a unified network. The resulting template embeddings serve as class prototypes and are optimized jointly with the feature extractor under a distance-based classification objective. This ensures alignment between prototypes and sample embeddings, yielding more reliable confidence estimations. Experiments with ResNet and ViT backbones demonstrate that TRL achieves superior performance across multiple tasks, including out-of-distribution detection, misclassification detection, few-shot learning, and class-incremental learning. Code will be made available upon acceptance. © 2026 Elsevier B.V.
